    "physical_description": "Small woollen carpet.\r\n\r\nWARP: white wool; Z2S; 17 threads per inch (60 per dm).\r\n\nWEFT: brown wool; Z2S; 2 shoots after each row of knots; 14 knots per inch (56 per dm).\r\n\nPILE: wool: 6 colours: red, dark blue, blue, pink, brown, white; asymmetrical knot open to the right and tied around 2 threads; there are 2 symmetrical knots at the end of each row; 119 knots per sq. inch (1680 per sq. dm.\r\n\nSIDE FINISH: one cord over sewn with blue wool.\r\n\nEND FINISH: lower: 2 cms. plain weave with 2 shoots of red wool, the rest white.  Upper: 2.5 cms. plain weave with white wool wefts.\r\n\r\nDESIGN: Field: red ground with 10 bands of 4 guls quartered and outlined in dark blue, with the top 3 bands in blue.  At the centre of each gul is a red rectangle in a white diamond within a red and blue quartered rectangle that extends in trefoils and a bar into the quarters of pink and white.  The blue of the rectangle extends in a fine line horizontally and vertically to form an all over grid.  Offset between the guls on a fine brown and white vertical lines is a secondary motif of a blunt hooked cross in blue within a pink stepped lozenge.\r\n\r\nMain border: red ground with alternate pink and white octagons each containing a rosette and surrounded by small blue triangles and, on the side borders, abutting each other but along the upper and lower borders divided by a line of diagonal blocks of colour which elsewhere form the guard stripes.\r\n\r\nInner and outer borders: a row of stylised flowers and 2 half rows, all composed of coloured blocks.  Along both sides the outermost guard stripe is continued to the end.\r\n\r\nLower and upper band: a red ground with closely-drawn lattice of toothed lines in blue, white and pink; each lozenge created by these lines contains 4 tiny white florets.  Above and below this panel is a narrow border of diagonal blocks of colour.",
